ing two-login Chromium journey. A supported CDP Network observer retains actual established-socket closure independently of Playwright's per-document map. Denied requests, removed editor, surviving-login continuity, forwarded queued writes, no later frames and saved/reloaded native content remain required. No application authorization or transport policy changes.\n\n## 📌 Current candidate\n\nSource **8177c1466ace555817cf2dbb9a2e5f2b5abc2c62**, tree **700d5792fa46342491f9c970d01b06dbf4ccfaa4**, actual base **89e4426dfff1c3469b260305e21180ffd79fdb7f**. 37 files, 3232 additions and 126 deletions. Complete M outcome, exact ticket title and landing bookkeeping preserved; next159, grooming date unchanged, completion counter148/145/149. Only SPN149 is removed; index generated by CLI.\n\nBoth independent nonimplementing reviewers (`/root/spn149_grade_a` and `/root/spn149_grade_b`) scored exact **8177c1466ace555817cf2dbb9a2e5f2b5abc2c62** **100/100**, each **35/25/20/10/10**, with no actionable findings or remaining steps to 100. Each independently passed all 19 focused controls under the pinned Node, serial runner and watchdog (A: 169 ms; B: 171 ms; RSS unsampled because both ended before the 200 ms monitor tick). Each verified all 37 changed-file original/masked hashes, the complete diff, dependency/source equivalence and retained receipts. No CI-result deduction or exception. Required current-source hosted acceptance remains **pending**. No product UI change; visual approval is inapplicable.\n\nThe first review intake exposed old numerical grades in a historical record. Neither reviewer issued a qualifying grade; their technical reports and one focused-control receipt are retained. Final grading restarted with two fresh independent reviewers and a hash-bound packet that masks only historical numerical grades/rubrics/points in two files. All technical content and the complete source diff remained inspectable; no candidate change or discarded grade was involved. The validation archive will preserve both final reports and this intake disposition.\n\n## 🧪 Local evidence and limits\n\n[Maintained local receipts](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/blob/8177c1466ace555817cf2dbb9a2e5f2b5abc2c62/docs/implementation/evidence/SPN-149/current-main-20261114/checks.json) preserve all commands, source/dependency hashes and logs.19 focused observer/authority/cleanup/routing controls passed; dependency boundaries, targeted lint/format, full TypeScript, backlog and exact-title PR checks passed. Full TypeScript8465ms peak1652704KiB with tool-only GOMEMLIMIT1GiB/GOMAXPROCS2 under the unchanged2GiB watchdog. Commands under200ms have unsampled RSS. Final PR check493ms181600KiB. No local browser execution; native acceptance remains owned by existing development/production Chromium cases.\n\nAll three ticket executable files are unchanged from the preserved prior implementation; current-main merge conflicts were only bookkeeping. The initial fixed two-sample native investigation remains closed: natural observation gap not reproduced; a separately controlled pinned-runtime probe demonstrated the conditional page-map gap. Neither proves historical event ordering. No assertion retry, timeout increase or unchanged-workflow rerun is part of this integration.\n\n## ⚠️ Preserved first failures\n\n[Prior immutable acceptance and failure history](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/blob/9392210d92f3ae706443ca49803c4ea7122322af/docs/implementation/evidence/SPN-149/acceptance/acceptance.json) preserves earlier source/check/review identities. Old64d85 CI43373411759 failed its selected development2/2 gate after a Space guest export-snapshot reset and cancellation; cause/first-attempt timeline/cancellation trigger remain unproved. The separate scope assessment is retained and no speculative Space export repair is absorbed here.\n\nSPN158 CI43553620429 production1 job132321620858 supplies a new old-page-counter recurrence at sourcebfeb0b23/tested1211f269: first attempt7559ms failed the unchanged5000ms closure poll; configured retry1 passed5996ms and failOnFlakyTests correctly failed the worker. Sign-in was visible; later queued-write assertions were not reached, and only retry1 retained a trace. Artifact 14097746136 (SHA-256 `d30a17c29b5eb10716abed4873159e7df71c2949cfd378ce7f54efeed5e22410`) and its first-failure report, screenshots, source and terminal outcomes are preserved in the [immutable SPN-158 record](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/tree/0cadd4707e659fcc79b26f15ea9802fb7fd45e7f/docs/review-assets/spn-158-validation-bfeb0b23). This is separate evidence, not proof of cause. SPN-158’s restore repair is not imported.\n\n## 🚦 Validation and completion record\n\nThe pre-push checkpoint above is superseded only by the exact immutable [validation archive](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/tree/archive/spn-149-validation-8177c146-20261114/docs/review-assets/spn-149-validation-8177c146) when published. Missing archives are pending evidence, never a pass. It will account for exact reviewed/tested/base identities, all seven required gates, every selected worker, first failures and source limits. Keep this PR draft until all applicable acceptance succeeds and actual main remains current.\n\nAfter qualifying guarded squash merge, the [completion archive](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/tree/archive/spn-149-completion-8177c146-20261114/docs/review-assets/spn-149-completion-8177c146) will record the verified squash/tree identity, preserved unique work and exact-head/active-PR guarded cleanup of obsolete implementation/integration/evidence refs. Current cleanup remains pending; prior capability limitations are historical and will be rechecked.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-13T04:15:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T05:07:03Z","closed_at":"2026-11-14T05:07:01Z","merged_at":"2026-11-14T05:07:01Z","merge_commit_sha":"a3dfc6f3373babecf979d5b851bbbf46c6dbb3b9","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"re